cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MetriPlane, please cite the software release."
title: "MetriPlane: Open Research Software for Camera-First Planar Metric State Streaming, Replay, and Zone Analytics"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Parkkinen"
    given-names: "Miko"
version: "0.1.4"
date-released: "2026-06-10"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Miko997/metriplane"
url: "https://github.com/Miko997/metriplane"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20631037"
abstract: >-
  MetriPlane is open research software for camera-first planar metric state
  streaming, deterministic replay, and zone analytics. The software detects
  fiducial markers, maps observations into metric XY coordinates, supports
  multi-camera fusion and tracking, computes zone analytics, streams
  schema-versioned WebSocket state, records JSONL sessions, and packages
  reproducibility artifacts such as manifests, checksums, and deterministic
  replay workflows. The v0.1.4 release stabilizes the public repository layout
  and preserves the v0.1.3 benchmark evidence values.
keywords:
  - research software
  - digital twins
  - robotics
  - industrial automation
  - physical observability
  - deterministic replay
  - zone analytics
  - ArUco
  - planar homography
  - reproducibility
